  {
    "number": 103985,
    "title": "Abort GPU communicators concurrently to avoid getting stuck.",
    "user": "copybara-service[bot]",
    "created_at": "2025-11-07T21:24:36",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-07T21:24:36",
    "body": "Abort GPU communicators concurrently to avoid getting stuck.\n\nRecall that when a GPU PjRt client detects that a process has failed, it will\nattempt to abort all communicators with that process as a participant.\nPreviously, the communicators were aborted serially, but this was leading to a\ndeadlock.\n\nConsider a deployment with three processes: A, B, and C. There are two\ncommunicators: one for A, B, and C and one for A and C. Imagine C fails during\na collective on the ABC communicator. If process A attempts to abort the AC\ncommunicator before the ABC communicator, the cancellation of the AC\ncommunicator gets blocked by the pending collective, and the collective is\nnever cancelled because the ABC communicator is not aborted until after the AC\ncommunicator.\n\nThis commit changes the aborts to happen concurrently and was suggested by the\nNCCL team. Emprically, it has solved the problem so far.\n",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/103985",
    "files": [
      {
        "filename": "third_party/xla/xla/backends/gpu/collectives/BUILD",
        "additions": 1,
        "deletions": 0
      },
      {
        "filename": "third_party/xla/xla/backends/gpu/collectives/gpu_cliques.cc",
        "additions": 38,
        "deletions": 7
      }
    ]
  },
  {
