    "updated_at": "2025-11-07T18:03:06",
    "body": "PR #33656: [ROCm] Fix rocm device lib failure due to clash in include dirs\n\nImported from GitHub PR https://github.com/openxla/xla/pull/33656\n\n📝 Summary of Changes\nFix build error reported here: https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/33589\n\n🎯 Justification\nhttps://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/33589\nThe issue happens because we add the same directory twice once with the headr the second on as a directory itself\nto the sources of the genrule\n\n🚀 Kind of Contribution\nPlease remove what does not apply: 🐛 Bug Fix,\n\n📊 Benchmark (for Performance Improvements)\nNot relevant, build fix.\n\n🧪 Unit Tests:\nNot relevant build fix.\n\n🧪 Execution Tests:\nNot relevant build fix.\n\nCopybara import of the project:\n\n--\n7b05237a5003a39c4ef1e27cd455651c12aa7b60 by Alexandros Theodoridis <atheodor@amd.com>:\n\nFix rocm device lib failure due to clash in include dirs\n\n--\ndcc33693d2ec741321025eb6546546cdd445f6f3 by Alexandros Theodoridis <atheodor@amd.com>:\n\nUse paths to extract the include paths from the hdrs\n\n--\n588ef972239cda0a9216fb3bb89ed98ec8da65b0 by Alexandros Theodoridis <atheodor@amd.com>:\n\nTranform to custom bazel rule\n\nMerging this change closes #33656\n\nFUTURE_COPYBARA_INTEGRATE_REVIEW=https://github.com/openxla/xla/pull/33656 from ROCm:fix_rocm_device_lib_failure 588ef972239cda0a9216fb3bb89ed98ec8da65b0\n",
